{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBTr13372jK1d71Eetyb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 0** (Fe 0.84, Sb 0.16), which had the highest EQE of the three compositions I measured: **0.108%**. The EQE figures are percentages.\n\nI used all 3 merit measurements. Each step up in iron content gave a higher EQE:\n\n| Index | Fe fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 13 | 0.52 | 0.005 |\n| 4 | 0.76 | 0.040 |\n| 0 | 0.84 | 0.108 |\n\nMy reading is that iron-rich, hematite-like oxide is what absorbs light at 2.7 eV. The films near a 1:1 iron-to-antimony ratio (the FeSbO4 region) performed poorly. None of the Sb-rich half of the library (indices 14–29) was measured, so the claim that it's worse rests on the trend, not on data.\n\n- **Peak position is uncertain:** because EQE was still rising at the iron-rich edge, the true peak is probably at index 0 or nearby. Indices 1–3 weren't measured, so one of them could be slightly better.\n- **Structures unconfirmed:** I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements, so which crystal phases are present hasn't been checked. Those measurements wouldn't have changed the score, which counts only EQE."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_read_input_tokens":8181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":467},"output_tokens":440,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2278fc8a-5462-49a3-96f1-ba4aeec7aa15","uuid":"aca20eb7-160c-401c-978a-adbb75a37b18","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:33:29.129Z","request_id":"req_011CfBTqzZGGRcV86pE9GX6J"}
